  "title": "Canada's Top Court Upholds Quebec Religious Symbols Ban",
  "summary": "The Canadian Supreme Court upheld Quebec's ban on public sector workers wearing religious symbols, including hijabs and turbans, despite criticism of the policy's implications on religious freedom and civil rights. The ruling reflects a broader push for secularism.",
